{"slug":"ted-strickland","qid":"Q465295","name":"Ted Strickland","desc":"American politician (born 1941)","article":"Ted Strickland","born":"1941-08-04","died":null,"birthplace":"Lucasville","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"Governor of Ohio","w":"","f":2007,"u":2011},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"OH-06","f":1997,"u":2007},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"OH-06","f":1993,"u":1995}],"summary":"Theodore Strickland (born August 4, 1941) is an American politician who served as the 68th governor of Ohio from 2007 to 2011. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously represented Ohio's 6th congressional district in the United States House of Representatives from 1993 to 1995, and again from 1997 to 2007.\nA native of Lucasville, Ohio, Strickland earned degrees from Asbury University, Asbury Theological Seminary, and the University of Kentucky.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":2016,"o":"S","k":"OH","p":"D","v":1996908,"s":37.16,"w":false,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":2004,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":223842,"s":99.94,"w":true,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":2002,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":113972,"s":59.48,"w":true,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":2000,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":138849,"s":57.72,"w":true,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1998,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":102852,"s":56.96,"w":true,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1996,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":118003,"s":51.32,"w":true,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1994,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":87861,"s":49.05,"w":false,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":122720,"s":50.72,"w":true,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1980,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":84235,"s":45.4,"w":false,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1978,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":46318,"s":35.11,"w":false,"n":"Ted Strickland"},{"y":1976,"o":"H","k":"OH-06","p":"D","v":67067,"s":38.52,"w":false,"n":"Ted Strickland"}]}